{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Why your init service never starts",
  "hook": "How do `init.rc` actions, triggers and services decide what starts when?",
  "topic": "aosp/boot/init-rc-actions",
  "tags": [
    "aosp",
    "init",
    "debugging"
  ],
  "level": "intermediate",
  "series": "aosp-boot-sequence",
  "series_index": 2,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Defining a service does not necessarily start it.",
      "narration": "Your daemon exists on disk but never appears in process listings. First inspect its init service state, then find the installed service declaration.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Declared, not started",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sh",
          "text": "adb shell getprop init.svc.demo\nadb shell cat \\\n  /vendor/etc/init/demo.rc\n# Blank state? Check loading and name.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Use your actual service name",
            "Inspect the installed rc file"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "A disabled service needs an explicit start.",
      "narration": "This example declares a vendor daemon but disables automatic class startup. Oneshot prevents automatic restart after exit; neither option creates the executable or policy.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Read the service",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "android-init",
          "text": "service demo /vendor/bin/demo\n    class late_start\n    user system\n    disabled\n    oneshot",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Example rc; binary must exist",
            "SELinux domain must be configured"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Property triggers queue actions; action commands run in order.",
      "narration": "Add a property action that explicitly starts the service. Init queues matching actions and executes their commands in order; process readiness requires separate coordination.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Follow the trigger",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "android-init",
          "text": "on property:sys.boot_completed=1\n    start demo\n# Example action in the installed rc",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 30,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "before",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "Property matches",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 56,
          "w": 35,
          "h": 11,
          "color": "blue",
          "at": 1800,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "after",
          "type": "box",
          "text": "start demo",
          "x": 57,
          "y": 56,
          "w": 35,
          "h": 11,
          "color": "orange",
          "at": 2600,
          "enter": "pop"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "before",
          "to": "after",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "draw"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "start launches; it does not await readiness",
            "No global order across parallel daemons"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 76,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 20,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 4400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "A matched action can still fail to execute the daemon.",
      "narration": "After boot, inspect both the trigger and service state. If startup failed, init logs distinguish missing executables, permission failures, and invalid service configuration.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Check both outcomes",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "inspect",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sh",
          "text": "adb shell getprop sys.boot_completed\nadb shell getprop init.svc.demo\nadb logcat -b all -d -s init",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 34,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "checks",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "running: process was launched",
            "stopped: inspect exit and init logs"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 3400,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "takeaway": "A service declaration defines a process; a matching action or class start launches it.",
  "sources": [
    "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/core/+/refs/heads/main/init/README.md"
  ]
}
